  "description": "English Baroque architecture incorporates Baroque elements like grandeur and dramatic forms but with greater restraint, symmetry, and classical proportion, reflecting English sensibilities. It emerged after the Restoration of the monarchy in 1660, serving as a visual expression of royal power and national confidence after the austere Commonwealth period.",
